    "The text message does not confirm the roof cause, the repair cost or who pays.",
    "Logging JOB-101 does not assign a contractor or book a visit.",
    "The escalation does not confirm the oven is fixed or that the invoice is valid.",
    "The fence work is not on this oven ticket and was not verified."
  ],
  "remaining_work": [
    "Accounts/maintenance to reopen or verify NBL-024 and obtain the Lantern Works/Keystone work result and invoice before any payment (ESC-103).",
    "Confirm with the tenant whether the oven now works; correct the 'fence and oven fixed' message sent on 2026-08-26.",
    "Assign a contractor and visit for JOB-101 after the tenant replies with photos and details, within the 72-hour target.",
    "Landlord still needs telling about the roof leak and the oven closure."
  ],
  "missing_info": [
    "Invoice amount, issuer and who pays.",
    "Whether the oven was repaired and by whom.",
    "Whether the Keystone Solutions invoice relates to this job.",
    "Tenant's photos and whether the leak is near electrics.",
    "Whether the fence work was ever on this ticket."
  ],
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "severity": "urgent",
  "summary": "The oven ticket was closed as completed without payment, with no verified work result, while an invoice from an unclear provider sits on the record. The tenant's new roof-leak report was logged as urgent ticket JOB-101, and the tenant was texted with a 72-hour target and safety advice. Accounts was asked to verify the oven closure and invoice before any payment.",
  "answers": [
    {
      "question": "Where does this case stand right now, and what is outstanding?",
      "answer": "The oven job is marked completed and closed without payment, but nothing verifies the repair. An invoice was received with no amount or issuer, and the provider is inconsistent (Lantern Works assigned, Keystone Solutions named). The tenant's roof leak is a new issue, now JOB-101. Outstanding: verify the oven job and invoice, confirm the oven works, assign and visit for the roof leak, and tell the landlord."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the next action, who is it for, and through which channel?",
      "answer": "Text to Imogen Clarke by SMS on 07700 900512 confirming JOB-101 and the 72-hour target, with safety advice (done). Internal escalation to accounts to verify the oven closure and invoice before any payment (done). Next: chase the tenant for photos, and message the landlord about the roof leak and the oven closure."
    },
    {
      "question": "Does anything need a human decision, and why?",
      "answer": "Yes. Whether to reopen the oven job and whether any invoice is payable needs accounts/maintenance, because the amount, issuer and work result are unverified and the closure conflicts with the invoice. The fence/oven message to the tenant also needs correcting by a person."
    }
  ],
  "actions_claimed": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "A1",
      "description": "Created urgent roof repair ticket JOB-101 for the conservatory leak."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A2",
      "description": "Sent SMS to tenant Imogen Clarke confirming JOB-101, the 72-hour target and safety advice."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A3",
      "description": "Escalated ESC-103 to accounts to verify the oven closure, invoice and provider."
    }
  ],
  "failed_actions": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "escalate_to_human (first attempt)",
      "handling": "Validation failed (missing options and recommendation); resent with both fields and succeeded as ESC-103 (A3)."
    }
  ],
  "conflicts": [
    "Event 016 tells the tenant 'the fence and oven have both been fixed', but the oven ticket has no work result and the fence is not on it.",
    "Ticket closed 'without payment' (event 030), yet an invoice was received (event 017).",
    "Lantern Works was assigned (event 011), but the closure note cites Keystone Solutions (event 029).",
    "Ticket shows stage completed but the keys and priority validation errors repeat (events 022-028); no clean close record."
  ]
}

